# ToolSuite Pro

60+ free, privacy-first browser tools — PDF, image, conversion, calculators and more. Everything runs client-side; no files are ever uploaded to a server.

## Deploy to Vercel

### Option A — Vercel CLI (fastest)

```bash
npm i -g vercel
vercel
```

Follow the prompts. On first deploy Vercel will ask:
- **Set up and deploy?** → Y
- **Which scope?** → your account
- **Link to existing project?** → N
- **Project name** → toolsuite (or anything you like)
- **In which directory is your code located?** → `./` (current directory)

Vercel auto-detects the `outputDirectory: "public"` from `vercel.json` — no build step needed.

### Option B — Vercel Dashboard (drag & drop)

1. Go to [vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new)
2. Click **"Import Git Repository"** — or drag the entire project folder onto the dashboard
3. Leave all build settings blank (no framework, no build command)
4. Set **Output Directory** to `public`
5. Click **Deploy**

### Option C — GitHub → Vercel (recommended for ongoing updates)

1. Push this folder to a GitHub repo
2. Go to [vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new) → Import the repo
3. Vercel reads `vercel.json` automatically — click **Deploy**
4. Every `git push` to `main` triggers a new deployment

## Project structure

```
toolsuite-vercel/
├── public/
│   ├── index.html      ← The entire app (single file)
│   ├── robots.txt
│   └── sitemap.xml
├── vercel.json         ← Routing, headers, cache rules
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

## After deploying

1. **Custom domain** — Vercel Dashboard → your project → Settings → Domains → Add
2. **Update canonical URL** — replace `https://toolsuite.vercel.app` in `index.html` and `sitemap.xml` with your real domain
3. **Update sitemap** — change the `<loc>` URL to match your domain

## What's configured

| Feature | Detail |
|---|---|
| Routing | All paths → `index.html` (SPA-style) |
| Cache | HTML: no-cache (always fresh) · assets: 24h |
| Security headers | CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options |
| SEO | Meta description, Open Graph, Twitter Card, sitemap, robots.txt |
| HTTPS | Automatic via Vercel (Let's Encrypt) |
